  "question": {
    "text": "A thin circular ring of mass $\\mathrm{m}$ and radius $\\mathrm{R}$ is rotating about its axis with a constant angular velocity $\\omega$. Two objects each of mass $M$ are attached gently to the opposite ends of a diameter of the ring. The ring now rotates with an angular velocity $\\omega^{\\prime}=$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EXmgJ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\omega \\mathrm{m}}{(\\mathrm{m}+2 \\mathrm{M})}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "G1s9V",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\omega(\\mathrm{m}+2 \\mathrm{M})}{\\mathrm{m}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IClwi",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\omega(m-2 M)}{(m+2 M)}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8lo6k",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\omega m}{(m+M)}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$L_i=L_f$\n$m R R^2 \\omega=\\left(m R^2+2 M R^2\\right) \\omega^{\\prime}$\n$\\omega^{\\prime}=\\left(\\frac{m \\omega}{m+2 M}\\right)$",
    "image": null
